  "actions": {
    "source": "exec-de3b7a89-aa64-4b5d-a539-291899c91e76.png",
    "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. NEW animation sheet of the SAME fire harlequin in this reference, same clean bold anime cartoon cel shading, simplified readable shapes, red/black diamond suit, ONE cone cap, white ruff, pale face red nose, curled shoes, gold cuffs. Ragged torn crimson cape of late battle. Exactly FOUR columns by FIVE rows =20 complete LEFT-facing figures, transparent alpha, generous gaps. No background, haze, floor, panels or text. Every figure full body including all extremities. Consistent body scale, each cell taller than wide.\nRow1 ULTIMATE CHARGE 4 frames: wide planted stance, both hands gather a small orange diamond flame near chest; palms cupped pulling it closer; head down teeth clenched with cape lifted; straighten leaning forward holding concentrated flame ready to push. Cape and cap flutter differently each frame.\nRow2 EMBER LOB 4 frames: gather glowing fire orb at chest; raise throwing LEFT arm far above head with torso twisted; throw overhead forward LEFT, extended arm fingers release orange ember; arm follows through low and cape whips right. Clearly distinct throwing action.\nRow3 GROUND FIRE 4 frames: raise one fist above head; crouch rapidly winding up; slam gloved palm against ground at left foot, orange flame attached to palm; rise from low crouch with hand extended. Dynamic cape.\nRow4 KNOCKBACK 4 frames: recoil backward facing left arms shielding face; airborne flung backward to right torso tilted; tumbling sideways cape whipping; almost horizontal falling with limbs extended. Do not shrink character relative to standing poses.\nRow5 RECOVERY 4 frames: lying prone fully on side, still, defeated; sitting propped on one elbow; pushing up with one knee planted; standing hunched tired. 20 figures only. Preserve tasteful costume and no gore. True transparency not a painted checkerboard.",
